WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:10.410
Clerk: Welcome to GameYield...

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.713
...what would you like
to pre-order today?

00:00:12.713 --> 00:00:14.615
Pollychester: Oh...no,
I just wanted to buy...

00:00:14.615 --> 00:00:16.516
...the new Phthalamon game.

00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:18.085
Clerk: Let me check.

00:00:18.085 --> 00:00:19.887
Ah, OK.

00:00:19.887 --> 00:00:23.524
Do you want Phthalamon
Polyethylene or Polystyrene?

00:00:23.524 --> 00:00:24.925
Pollychester:
What's the difference?

00:00:24.925 --> 00:00:27.527
Clerk: Well, if you want to
catch all the Phthalamon,

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:29.730
you have to trade
with a friend...

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:33.567
...or if you're sad and lonely,
you can buy both.

00:00:33.567 --> 00:00:36.303
Pollychester: I'll go
with Polystyrene...

00:00:36.303 --> 00:00:38.639
...because the one on
the front looks better.

00:00:38.639 --> 00:00:39.806
Clerk: Everyone does...

00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:42.976
Pollymer: Yes!

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:44.311
Game time!

00:00:44.311 --> 00:00:45.779
What are we playing today?

00:00:45.779 --> 00:00:51.318
Phthalamon Polystyrene
Edition, eh?

00:00:51.318 --> 00:00:52.819
All right!

00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:54.087
See you in there!

00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:56.290
Gotta plasticize 'em all!

00:00:56.290 --> 00:00:58.625
Plastikos: Hello there.

00:00:58.625 --> 00:01:01.028
Welcome to the
world of Phthalamon!

00:01:01.028 --> 00:01:03.997
People call me the
Phthalamon professor.

00:01:03.997 --> 00:01:07.100
This world is inhabited
by Phthalamon.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:10.437
They come from chemicals
called phthalates, and

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:14.107
they are used to change
the properties of plastics.

00:01:14.107 --> 00:01:17.778
People use phthalates for
all sorts of purposes:

00:01:17.778 --> 00:01:19.446
they can soften plastic,...

00:01:19.446 --> 00:01:22.416
...make it more flexible,...

00:01:22.416 --> 00:01:25.385
...make plastic
more transparent,...

00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:27.354
...or to increase plastic's...

00:01:27.354 --> 00:01:29.189
...durability.

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:30.090
Me?

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:31.959
I study Phthalamon.

00:01:31.959 --> 00:01:36.129
Your own Phthalamon
adventure is about to begin.

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:37.297
Here's two Phthalamon.

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:39.766
My assistant,
Pollymer, will help you.

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:41.101
Pollychester: But what
will you be doing?

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:42.769
Plastikos: Don't
worry about that.

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:43.770
Go on!

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:46.273
Pollymer: You heard him,
there's a lot to do.

00:01:46.273 --> 00:01:48.141
Pollychester: Hey! Wait!

00:01:48.141 --> 00:01:50.444
I knew I should have
picked up the guide...

00:01:50.444 --> 00:01:52.479
What are we even looking for?

00:01:52.479 --> 00:01:53.880
Phthalamon!

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:57.250
They're used in making
plastics, and can be found

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:58.952
almost everywhere!

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:00.020
You can find them...

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:01.321
...around toys,...

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:02.589
...food packaging,...

00:02:02.589 --> 00:02:04.324
...medical bags and tubing,...

00:02:04.324 --> 00:02:05.659
...plastic coatings,...

00:02:05.659 --> 00:02:08.729
...and even some products that
aren't made of plastic.

00:02:08.729 --> 00:02:11.498
Buy an overly
expensive vinyl toy?

00:02:11.498 --> 00:02:12.532
Phthalates.

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:14.568
Like that "new car" smell?

00:02:14.568 --> 00:02:15.936
Phthalates in the air.

00:02:15.936 --> 00:02:18.905
Feel how smooth your
hair is after shampooing?

00:02:18.905 --> 00:02:20.707
Phthalates in the shampoo.

00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:24.077
Like the feel of that slick,
plastic video game system?

00:02:24.077 --> 00:02:24.745
Phthalates.

00:02:24.745 --> 00:02:26.446
Wait...what?

00:02:26.446 --> 00:02:27.814
Let's see what you got.

00:02:27.814 --> 00:02:29.249
Let a Phthalamon out.

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:35.656
Diisononyl: DIISO!

00:02:35.656 --> 00:02:37.958
Pollymer: That's Diisononyl
Phthalate!

00:02:37.958 --> 00:02:38.792
It's a pretty...

00:02:38.792 --> 00:02:40.660
...common plasticizer.

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:42.329
Pollychester: Plasticizer?

00:02:42.329 --> 00:02:45.132
Pollymer: Sure, any chemical
that gives plastics that

00:02:45.132 --> 00:02:46.033
flexible,...

00:02:46.033 --> 00:02:47.501
...smooth quality...

00:02:47.501 --> 00:02:50.737
...we like in products
is called a plasticizer.

00:02:50.737 --> 00:02:52.672
Pollychester: Aw, it's cute too.
Diisononyl: Iiiiisoooo....

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:54.474
Pollymer: I wouldn't do that...

00:02:54.474 --> 00:02:56.076
...he may cause cancer.

00:02:56.076 --> 00:02:59.479
The state of California
recognizes diisononyl as

00:02:59.479 --> 00:03:00.647
a carcinogen.

00:03:00.647 --> 00:03:02.916
Pollychester: Why would the
professor study phthalates

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:04.117
if they are dangerous?!

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:06.420
Pollymer: That's exactly why.

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:09.623
Phthalamon are everywhere,
but we aren't sure how much

00:03:09.623 --> 00:03:10.957
they affect us.

00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:13.527
Pollymer: Some phthalates may
increase the risk of getting

00:03:13.527 --> 00:03:15.529
certain kinds of cancers...

00:03:15.529 --> 00:03:18.198
...and others may be endocrine
disruptors.

00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:20.367
Pollychester: Is this one of
those educational games that

00:03:20.367 --> 00:03:23.437
grandparents
accidentally give to kids?

00:03:23.437 --> 00:03:25.972
Pollymer: Your endocrine
system is a complex group of

00:03:25.972 --> 00:03:27.441
chemicals in your body...

00:03:27.441 --> 00:03:30.343
...turning on and off chemical
reactions that keep things

00:03:30.343 --> 00:03:32.179
relatively normal in you.

00:03:32.179 --> 00:03:35.315
Things like your growth rate,
blood sugar levels, and

00:03:35.315 --> 00:03:38.218
internal temperature are
all regulated with help from

00:03:38.218 --> 00:03:39.553
your endocrine system.

00:03:39.553 --> 00:03:41.822
the phthalates that
are endocrine disrupters

00:03:41.822 --> 00:03:42.889
get in your body...

00:03:42.889 --> 00:03:45.459
...and block or imitate
endocrine chemicals.

00:03:45.459 --> 00:03:48.328
Pollychester: So how
do we find Phthalamon?

00:03:48.328 --> 00:03:50.530
Aren't they in the plastic?

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:52.899
Pollymer: Yeah, but
phthalates don't actually

00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:54.367
bind to the plastic.

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:57.237
Plastics are made of an
interlocking web of large

00:03:57.237 --> 00:03:59.172
molecules, called polymers.

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:02.075
Trapped inside the polymers
are other chemicals,

00:04:02.075 --> 00:04:03.076
like phthalates.

00:04:03.076 --> 00:04:05.479
Phthalates are much
smaller chemicals, and

00:04:05.479 --> 00:04:07.047
they're just mixed in there.

00:04:07.047 --> 00:04:10.517
So, if the plastic is heated,
cut up, or dissolved...

00:04:10.517 --> 00:04:13.353
...the polymers loosen, and
out come the phthalates!

00:04:13.353 --> 00:04:16.857
Phenol and Petrol:
HAHAHAHAHAHA!!!!!

00:04:16.857 --> 00:04:18.058
Pollychester: Who was that?

00:04:18.058 --> 00:04:21.261
Phenol: To cover the
world in plastic sheen.

00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:24.631
Petrol: To wrap your stuff,
and keep it clean.

00:04:24.631 --> 00:04:29.102
Phenol: To create any
shape your hearts desire.

00:04:29.102 --> 00:04:32.973
Petrol: To cast old
materials into the fire.

00:04:32.973 --> 00:04:34.574
Phenol: Phenol!

00:04:34.574 --> 00:04:35.742
Petrol: Petrol!

00:04:35.742 --> 00:04:39.980
Phenol: Team Plastics,
truly a sight to behold!

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:43.783
Petrol: Don't mess with
us, we break the mold!

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:45.252
Malleowth: Malleowth!

00:04:45.252 --> 00:04:46.620
Dat's bold!

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:49.389
Pollymer: Oh gosh,
not these guys...

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:50.457
What do you want?

00:04:50.457 --> 00:04:53.493
Petrol: We know you've
caught rare Phthalamon!

00:04:53.493 --> 00:04:57.130
Phenol: They can help
us create more plastics!

00:04:57.130 --> 00:05:01.001
Malleowth: So give 'em
up or pay da price!

00:05:03.737 --> 00:05:05.338
Pollychester: What the heck?

00:05:05.338 --> 00:05:09.342
Petrol: When you lose, we're
taking your Phthalamon.

00:05:09.342 --> 00:05:10.677
Pollychester: You don't get it!

00:05:10.677 --> 00:05:12.379
We have to study them...

00:05:12.379 --> 00:05:15.348
...we can't just keep cranking
out more plastics without

00:05:15.348 --> 00:05:17.717
understanding what
effects they have on us.

00:05:17.717 --> 00:05:20.187
Malleowth: Boring!

00:05:20.187 --> 00:05:21.188
Get 'im!

00:05:21.188 --> 00:05:23.089
Phenol: Go, Benzylbutyl!

00:05:23.089 --> 00:05:27.460
Benzylbutyl: Benzzzzzzyl!

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:28.528
Petrol: Go, Diethyl!

00:05:28.528 --> 00:05:30.564
Diethy: Ethyl!

00:05:30.564 --> 00:05:31.097
Pollymer: Hey!

00:05:31.097 --> 00:05:33.166
Two on one's not fair!

00:05:33.166 --> 00:05:35.635
Malleowth: She
missed da point...

00:05:35.635 --> 00:05:38.672
...we're da bad guys!

00:05:38.672 --> 00:05:39.406
Pollymer: Watch out...

00:05:39.406 --> 00:05:42.442
Benzylbutyl phthalate is
common in soft plastics.

00:05:42.442 --> 00:05:45.278
It can be found in
road cones, vinyl toys,

00:05:45.278 --> 00:05:46.279
and fake leather.

00:05:46.279 --> 00:05:49.316
It’s illegal to use Phtha-
lamon in Europe

00:05:49.316 --> 00:05:51.685
Pollychester: What
about the gassy one?

00:05:51.685 --> 00:05:53.453
Pollymer: That’s
Diethyl phthalate.

00:05:53.453 --> 00:05:55.088
It binds to perfumes.

00:05:55.088 --> 00:05:58.892
Odds are, if you smell something
“nice”, diethyl’s there.

00:05:58.892 --> 00:06:00.427
There are also concerns about

00:06:00.427 --> 00:06:02.395
its effects on our
nervous system.

00:06:02.395 --> 00:06:04.231
Send out a Phthalamon!

00:06:04.231 --> 00:06:04.965
Pollychester: Right...

00:06:04.965 --> 00:06:07.867
Dicotyl...I choose you!

00:06:07.867 --> 00:06:09.469
Dicotyl: Cotyl!

00:06:09.469 --> 00:06:10.136
Pollymer: Wow!

00:06:10.136 --> 00:06:11.705
You're really lucky!

00:06:11.705 --> 00:06:13.440
That's Dicotyl Terephthalate!

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:17.577
That Pthalamon uses plant oils
instead of synthetic chemicals.

00:06:17.577 --> 00:06:20.647
It's a natural alternative
to other phthalates, and

00:06:20.647 --> 00:06:24.084
reasearch suggests they don't
have the same health concerns.

00:06:24.084 --> 00:06:25.952
Petrol: Awww, it's cute.

00:06:25.952 --> 00:06:27.754
Pollychester: Show 'em, Dicotyl!

00:06:27.754 --> 00:06:30.924
Dicotyl: DICOTYL!!!!!

00:06:30.924 --> 00:06:32.993
Phenol: No way!

00:06:32.993 --> 00:06:34.961
These kids aren't
playing around!

00:06:35.595 --> 00:06:38.331
Petrol: Show them
what we've got!

00:06:38.331 --> 00:06:39.232
Diethylhexyl: Hexyl...

00:06:39.232 --> 00:06:41.635
Go, Diethylhexyl Phthalate!

00:06:41.635 --> 00:06:42.502
Pollychester: Woah...

00:06:42.502 --> 00:06:45.272
Pollymer: That's a
legendary Phthalamon!

00:06:45.272 --> 00:06:47.907
It's effect is seen
in most plastics.

00:06:47.907 --> 00:06:52.512
Polyvinyl chloride, or PVC,
is a very common plastic.

00:06:52.512 --> 00:06:54.848
If a plastic is PVC,...

00:06:54.848 --> 00:06:57.317
...Diethylhexyl was involved.

00:06:57.317 --> 00:07:01.421
It's a cheap phthalate to use,
but it also has health concerns.

00:07:01.421 --> 00:07:02.622
This one's tough...

00:07:02.622 --> 00:07:04.257
Pollychester: Get it, Dicotyl!

00:07:04.257 --> 00:07:06.126
Dicotyl: DICOT...yl....

00:07:06.126 --> 00:07:09.062
Pollymer: It looks like Dicotyl
Terephthalate may be a powerful

00:07:09.062 --> 00:07:12.966
plasticizer, but it's also
expensive to use.

00:07:12.966 --> 00:07:15.635
Diethylhexyl: Diethyl...

00:07:15.635 --> 00:07:16.903
Pollychester: NOOOO!!!!

00:07:16.903 --> 00:07:19.606
Petrol: Ready to give up, twerp?

00:07:19.606 --> 00:07:20.774
Pollychester: No way!

00:07:20.774 --> 00:07:22.075
Go, Diisononyl!

00:07:22.075 --> 00:07:24.311
Diisononyl: DIISO!

00:07:24.311 --> 00:07:25.945
Malleowth: It ain't dat tough...

00:07:25.945 --> 00:07:28.114
Phenol: It sure isn't.

00:07:28.114 --> 00:07:30.550
Diethylhexyl: Hexyl...

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:32.585
Pollychester: This
isn't working either!

00:07:32.585 --> 00:07:33.320
Pollymer: Wait!

00:07:33.320 --> 00:07:35.221
Look at Diisononyl!

00:07:37.324 --> 00:07:41.294
Hexamoll: [ROARS]

00:07:41.294 --> 00:07:43.296
Pollymer: The chemical
reaction of hydrogenation

00:07:43.296 --> 00:07:45.799
turned Diisononyl into Hexamoll!

00:07:45.799 --> 00:07:47.567
And look at its attacks!

00:07:47.567 --> 00:07:51.271
The harmful side effects
of Diisononyl are gone!

00:07:51.271 --> 00:07:54.541
Adding hydrogen to this
phthalate made it less reactive.

00:07:54.541 --> 00:07:57.744
This new phthalate could be
better than Diethylhexyl! 

00:07:57.744 --> 00:07:58.778
Pollychester: Hexamoll!

00:07:58.778 --> 00:08:01.014
Seismic malleability!

00:08:03.516 --> 00:08:04.150
Phenol: What?!

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:05.752
Diethylhexyl: Hex!

00:08:08.355 --> 00:08:10.623
Petrol: Uh...uh...uh...

00:08:10.623 --> 00:08:12.325
Petrol, Phenol, and Malleowth:
Looks like Team Plastic's

00:08:12.325 --> 00:08:14.661
melting away!
Hexamoll: [ROARS]

00:08:14.661 --> 00:08:16.196
Pollychester: It's
difficult to decide

00:08:16.196 --> 00:08:17.931
what to do about phthalates.

00:08:17.931 --> 00:08:21.334
The plastics that make things
like medical tubing save

00:08:21.334 --> 00:08:23.203
millions of lives.

00:08:23.203 --> 00:08:27.173
On the other hand, people who
need constant medical treatment

00:08:27.173 --> 00:08:29.008
are at greater
risk of the negative

00:08:29.008 --> 00:08:30.877
side effects of phthalates.

00:08:30.877 --> 00:08:34.814
they could stay in the plastic,
or they could get out and enter

00:08:34.814 --> 00:08:36.216
your body through your blood,...

00:08:36.216 --> 00:08:37.617
...eating food,...

00:08:37.617 --> 00:08:39.652
...or just breathing.

00:08:39.652 --> 00:08:42.822
Pollymer: But with work, we
can make our plastics safer.

00:08:42.822 --> 00:08:45.225
If we look for natural
alternatives...

00:08:45.225 --> 00:08:46.226
...like Dicotyl.

00:08:46.226 --> 00:08:46.993
Dicotyl: Cotyl!...

00:08:46.993 --> 00:08:47.894
Polymer: Or we
research methods...

00:08:47.894 --> 00:08:50.063
Pollymer: ...for creating
safer phthalates...

00:08:50.063 --> 00:08:51.564
...like Hexamoll
Hexamoll: [ROARS]...

00:08:51.564 --> 00:08:54.134
Pollymer: ...we can have our
plastics and minimize the risk.

00:08:54.134 --> 00:08:57.103
It may take money and time, but
it's better than surrounding

00:08:57.103 --> 00:08:59.939
ourselves with products
that have unknown effects.

00:08:59.939 --> 00:09:01.441
Pollychester:
There's also ways we can

00:09:01.441 --> 00:09:03.676
just avoid using plastics...

00:09:03.676 --> 00:09:06.012
...shop with a canvas bag,...

00:09:06.012 --> 00:09:10.450
...eat off of glass or ceramic
plates, and use metal flatware.

00:09:10.450 --> 00:09:13.520
Pollymer: And keep your plastics
away from heat in microwaves and

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:15.989
dishwashers that
break down plastics...

00:09:15.989 --> 00:09:17.157
...and release phthalates

00:09:17.157 --> 00:09:19.292
Pollymer: And don't chew
on your plastic stuff...

00:09:19.292 --> 00:09:22.262
...it's understandable
for a baby, but come on...

00:09:22.262 --> 00:09:25.799
Pollychester: So, we beat the
bad guys and learned a lot.

00:09:25.799 --> 00:09:27.333
Did I beat the game?

00:09:27.333 --> 00:09:29.602
Pollymer: Oh, you
never "beat" this game.

00:09:29.602 --> 00:09:31.938
There's post game
missions, you have to

00:09:31.938 --> 00:09:33.106
play the other version...

00:09:33.106 --> 00:09:35.975
...there's the tradeable
card game, in about 5 years

00:09:35.975 --> 00:09:39.479
they'll do a remake of this
game, you're never done.

00:09:39.479 --> 00:09:41.815
This is you now.

00:09:41.815 --> 00:09:42.382
Dicotyl: Dicotyl!

